Version 0.2.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-27

- Record meetings: microphone and desktop audio into an Opus file
- Record browser meetings source by source with the companion extension for
  Chromium-based browsers; its native messaging hosts are registered per user
- Optionally record every browser meeting automatically, with a Stop notification
- Name missing libraries and GStreamer plugins at startup
- Packages for Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora, openSUSE, Arch Linux and Alpine, built and
  tested with the same scripts locally and in CI

Version 0.1.1
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-15

- Fix transcript-click crashes and GTK label sizing warnings
- Keep participants visible and rejoin interrupted speech with inline interjections
- Preserve interjections in exports

Version 0.1.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-15

First release.

- Play Cassini portable meetings with a transcript that follows playback
- Click words and timestamps to seek
- Speaker filter, transcript chooser, search
- Summary view with action items and topics
- Audio integrity check (exact-opus-audio-v1)
- Export as text or WebVTT
